# FormDesign in Cursor

FormDesign is a page-layout app (an InDesign alternative). Its MCP server is `formdes` (`.cursor/mcp.json` starts `./formdes mcp`, which starts the engine when needed). Every change an agent makes shows live in the FormDesign window and can be undone.

- To make or change a layout from files and a brief, follow `.agents/skills/formdes-harness/SKILL.md`: intake, make_layout, preview, set_slots, export_document. Do not read the source files into context first; intake is cheaper.
- For anything the fast path does not cover, `find_commands` (by word or by domain such as table, swatch, type) and then `run_commands` with `[{command, params}]` as one undoable batch. Error replies name the fix: the nearest command id or the parameters the command takes.
- `show` moves the person's view to a page, zoom, panel or tool so they can follow.
- Risky steps (publishing a website, overwriting a file, packaging, printing, deleting several pages) may wait for the person to approve them in Window > Agent Connect. When a call says it was not approved, ask the person; do not retry in a loop.
- In a terminal, `./formdes cmd ID key=value` runs one engine command on the open document, `./formdes actions` lists everything FormDesign can do, and `./formdes tool NAME '{json}'` calls an MCP tool.
- For work on FormDesign's own code, read `CLAUDE.md` and `.agents/skills/formdes-skillset/SKILL.md` first.
